node_modules
dist
.git
# NOTE: .gitignore is deliberately NOT excluded.
#
# Tools that walk the source tree read it to know what to skip. Tailwind v4's
# automatic source detection is one of them: without .gitignore it scanned
# dist/, and because `vite build` runs the client pass first, the SSR pass then
# saw dist/client/assets/*.js and generated 81 utilities the client pass never
# did. The two passes produced different CSS, so `styles.css?url` resolved to a
# different content hash in each — SSR linked a stylesheet that was never
# emitted, and production served a 404 for its CSS.
#
# Keeping .gitignore in the build context makes the container build see the
# same ignore rules as a local one.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.log
.vscode
.cursorrules
npm-debug.log*
